00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:56.350
No, I just assumed they were like a schnauzer and a poodle.
没有，我只是猜它们就像雪纳瑞和贵宾犬的结合。

422
00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.170
That's exactly what they are.
它们确实就是那样。

423
00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:02.330
I mean, it's like a Labradoodle is like a Labrador and a poodle.
我的意思是，就像拉布拉多贵宾犬是拉布拉多和贵宾犬结合一样。

424
00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:05.030
I guess it didn't click for me what a schnoodle was.
我当时好像没反应过来雪纳多犬是什么意思。

425
00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:08.150
I didn't know you could mix a schnauzer and a poodle.
我不知道雪纳瑞和贵宾犬还能串种。

426
00:19:08.350 --> 00:19:09.090
I didn't either.
我也不知道。

427
00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.130
How does that work?
这到底是怎么操作的？

428
00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:11.910
I don't know, and I don't want to think about it.
我不知道，我也不想去细想。

429
00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:12.290
Okay.
好吧。

430
00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.150
But back to Bobby Ray for a second.
不过我们回过头来再聊一下鲍比·雷。

431
00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.710
So, you guys, we did an AT&T commercial.
各位，我们拍了个AT&T的广告。

432
00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:17.950
It's out in the world now.
现在已经播出了。

433
00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:19.010
You will have seen some of it.
你们应该已经看到一部分了。

434
00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:19.510
It's so good.
拍得太棒了。

435
00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:20.550
It's so funny, lady.
太搞笑了，女士。

436
00:19:20.810 --> 00:19:21.650
They're so fun.
他们真的很有趣。

437
00:19:21.770 --> 00:19:22.810
You did them as well.
你们也拍了。

438
00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:25.090
They've really gotten almost the entire caSt.
他们几乎把整个演员阵容都请到了。

439
00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:25.570
Yeah.
对啊。

440
00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:28.490
Well, we were on set one day, and we were just chatting.
有一天我们在片场，当时正闲聊着。

441
00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.010
I was asking him how his life is.
我问他最近过得怎么样。

442
00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:34.330
He has a very peaceful existence on this nice big property in West Virginia,
他在西弗吉尼亚州有一处宽敞舒适的房产，过着非常平静的生活，

443
00:19:34.330 --> 00:19:36.590
and we exchanged phone numbers.
然后我们交换了电话号码。

444
00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:40.190
And when I watched this, I was like, oh, my gosh.
当我看到这个的时候，我心想，天哪。

445
00:19:40.690 --> 00:19:43.350
Bobby Ray was in it and didn't even tell me.
鲍比·雷参演了居然都没告诉我。

446
00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:44.750
There you go.
就是这样。

447
00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:45.510
There you go.
就是这样。

448
00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:46.930
So, I texted him, and I was like,
所以，我给他发信息说，

449
00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.390
can you please share with us what it was like to be on the paper?
你能跟我们分享一下登上报纸是什么感觉吗？

450
00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:52.970
And he sent us in this lovely audio clip.
然后他给我们发来了这段可爱的音频剪辑。

451
00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:53.630
Let's hear it.
请讲吧。

452
00:19:54.630 --> 00:20:01.310
Hello to the office ladies, Angela and Jenna, and your loyal listeners.
向《Office Ladies》的两位女士，安吉拉和珍娜，以及所有忠实听众问好。

453
00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:04.950
This is Bobby Ray Schaefer, a.k.a.
我是鲍比·雷·谢弗，也就是

454
00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:08.110
Bob Vance, Vance Refrigeration.
范斯制冷的鲍勃·范斯。

455
00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:16.870
I'm pleased to join you today to talk about my experience filming the new TV show,
很高兴今天能来和大家聊聊我拍摄新电视剧的经历，

456
00:20:17.390 --> 00:20:18.170
The Paper.
《The Paper》。

457
00:20:18.170 --> 00:20:28.450
There I was, in my house, on the hill, in the woods, in West Virginia, minding my own business.
当时我在西弗吉尼亚州树林里山上的房子里，过着我自己的平静生活。

458
00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:37.510
And I was working on my autobiography, which I'm sure the listeners will delight in the title,
我当时正在写自传，我相信听众们一定会喜欢这本书的名字，

459
00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:42.050
