00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:06.570
Would I be interested?
问我有没有兴趣？

464
00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:11.870
Would I be available for a new Greg Daniels project?
问我有没有空参与格雷格·丹尼尔斯的新项目？

465
00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:16.770
Well, there's only one answer to that, and it is, of course, yes.
嗯，这个问题只有一个答案，那就是，当然有。

466
00:21:17.550 --> 00:21:23.610
So, I send back my availability is total.
于是我回复说我完全有时间。

467
00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:26.850
And then I had to wait for a while.
然后我就得等上一阵子。

468
00:21:27.070 --> 00:21:28.630
You know how that goes, ladies.
两位女士，你们懂的。

469
00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:34.150
And at the time, I had thought when I left L.A.
当时我想过，自我离开洛杉矶

470
00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:37.950
after 40 years of grinding, that I would never go back.
打拼了40年之后，我绝不会再回去了。

471
00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:47.130
But, of course, as I told the producer who contacted me, I've never said no to Greg Daniels, and I'm not going to start now.
但正如我告诉联系我的制片人那样，我从来没有拒绝过格雷格·丹尼尔斯，这次也不会破例。

472
00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:52.190
So, after about a month of, is it going to happen, is it not going to happen?
所以，经过大约一个月“到底能不能成”的纠结，

473
00:21:52.210 --> 00:22:00.090
And I found myself right back in the old mindset of, it is, it isn't, it is, it isn't.
我又回到了那种“能成、不成、能成、不成”的旧思维模式中。

474
00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:02.250
And, you know, that's torture for an actor.
你们知道的，这对演员来说简直是折磨。

475
00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:08.610
But after not having to go through it for a while, it was kind of fun to be back in it, to tell you the truth.
但有一段时间不用经历这些之后，说实话，重新经历这种感觉还挺有意思的。

476
00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:12.030
And the deal was closed.
然后合同就敲定了。

477
00:22:12.210 --> 00:22:13.410
The arrangements were made.
各项事宜都安排妥当了。

478
00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:17.950
And I found myself on a big old jet plane to the coaSt.
我坐上了一架飞往西海岸的大型老式喷气客机。

479
00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:29.630
I went to the set the next morning, and I'd say that was the biggest difference in the office and the paper, is that being on the universal lot.
第二天早上我去了片场，要说《办公室》和《The Paper》最大的不同，那就是它在环球影城外景地上。

480
00:22:29.810 --> 00:22:38.290
When I would walk out of my trailer, you know, the tour carts would come rolling by, and all the people were waving and staring and yelling.
当我走出房车时，游览观光车刚好开过，所有人都在挥手、盯着看、大喊大叫。

481
00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:40.910
And that was a new dimension to filming.
这给拍摄带来了一种全新的维度。

482
00:22:40.910 --> 00:22:46.550
But anyway, it was fantastic to be back in the Vance Refrigeration office.
不管怎样，能回到范斯制冷的办公室真是太棒了。

483
00:22:46.830 --> 00:23:00.570
As you know, details are key on the office, and they are, too, on the paper, because it was a perfect replica right down to a secretary and the whole office.
如你们所知，细节在《办公室》里至关重要，《The Paper》里也是如此，因为这里简直是个完美的复刻，连秘书和整个办公室都一模一样。

484
00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:05.530
You know, I really knew then what deja vu felt like.
那一刻我真的懂得了什么是似曾相识的感觉。

485
00:23:05.670 --> 00:23:07.550
I mean, you know, I'd been there before.
我的意思是，我以前去过那里。

486
00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:13.470
But it was delightful to see all the, there were many of the crew members.
但很高兴能见到所有……现场有许多老工作组人员。

487
00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:19.470
And the key guy, of course, other than Mr. Daniels, was Sergio, our caterer.
核心人物当然除了丹尼尔斯先生外，还有我们的餐饮主管塞尔吉奥。

488
00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:23.030
And he was there, and it was a delight to see him.
他也来了，见到他真是太高兴了。

489
00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:27.730
And Veda, the script supervisor, and Dave Rogers, the editor.
还有剧本总监维达，以及剪辑师戴夫·罗杰斯。

490
00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:29.930
And so it was like old home week.
所以这感觉就像是老友重逢的欢聚一周。

491
00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:37.790
And it was really just a wonderful feeling to be back involved with those great people, so talented.
能重新和这群才华横溢、伟大的人共事，这种感觉真的很美好。

492
00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:40.790
And Greg was directing the pilot.
格雷格亲自执导了试播集。

493
00:23:41.090 --> 00:23:44.870
And so I got to spend some quality time with him.
所以我得以和他在一块儿度过了一段美好的时光。

494
00:23:45.030 --> 00:23:47.410
And he had written a very smart, funny open.
他写了一个非常聪明、有趣的开场。

495
00:23:47.410 --> 00:23:48.990
I hope you'll all enjoy it.
希望大家都会喜欢。

496
00:23:49.630 --> 00:23:56.310
And the main reason I did it, of course, other than, you know, it was Greg, is the historical link with the office.
我接拍的主要原因，当然除了因为格雷格之外，就是与《办公室》的历史渊源。

497
00:23:56.710 --> 00:24:00.890
As you know, as many of you know, I've been doing a lot of fan shows.
如你们所知，你们很多人都知道，我一直在参加很多粉丝见面会活动。

498
00:24:01.150 --> 00:24:07.410
And I have to say, I'll say it again, we do have the greatest fans in television show history.
我必须得说，我再说一遍，我们确实拥有电视史上最棒的粉丝。

499
00:24:07.410 --> 00:24:13.490
And I want to thank you all very much for making us feel so treasured and cherished.
我想非常感谢大家让我们感到如此被珍视和宠爱。

500
00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:15.570
It's really, truly a great honor.
这真的是一项极大的荣誉。

501
00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:24.010
And it's been a blessing to be able to make people happy with just a photo and a signature.
而且仅仅通过一张照片和一个签名就能让人们开心，这真是一种福气。

502
00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:25.930
And you gave me that.
而你给了我这一切。

503
00:24:26.210 --> 00:24:30.750
So, office ladies, you're kicking butt, taking names.
所以，各位办公室女郎，你们干得漂亮，大显身手。

504
00:24:30.950 --> 00:24:31.510
Keep it up.
保持下去。

505
00:24:31.770 --> 00:24:32.770
Love you very much.
非常爱你们。

506
00:24:32.850 --> 00:24:33.530
And I'll see you.
回头见。

507
00:24:33.890 --> 00:24:34.490
Bye-bye.
拜拜。

508
00:24:35.490 --> 00:24:36.910
Oh, that's not great.
哦，那可不太妙。

509
00:24:37.410 --> 00:24:38.090
So great.
太棒了。

510
00:24:38.710 --> 00:24:40.550
I just loved all of that.
我刚才真的超喜欢所有这些。

511
00:24:40.690 --> 00:24:44.650
And I texted him thank you so much from the two of us.
我给他发了短信，代表我们两个向他表示非常感谢。

512
00:24:44.790 --> 00:24:46.930
And he said, well, Ange, thank you.
他说，好吧，安吉，谢谢你。

513
00:24:47.090 --> 00:24:49.850
And know that I forgive you for spitting on me.
还要知道我原谅你朝我吐口水。

514
00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:56.100
And I said, I said, when did I spit on you?
我说，我说，我什么时候朝你吐口水了？

515
00:24:56.180 --> 00:24:57.020
I'm so sorry.
我太抱歉了。

516
00:24:57.160 --> 00:24:58.320
I guess I'm a hot mess.
我猜我真是个糊涂蛋。

517
00:24:58.460 --> 00:25:01.320
I thought maybe I spit on him on the AT&T commercial.
我想也许是在拍AT&T广告时我朝他吐口水了。

518
00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:01.900
Okay.
好吧。

519
00:25:02.080 --> 00:25:04.720
And he wrote back and he said, ha-ha, fun run.
他回信说，哈哈，欢乐跑。

520
00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:07.260
I made a remark about the dead cat.
我提到了那只死猫。

521
00:25:07.420 --> 00:25:08.580
It was a deleted scene.
那是个删减片段。

522
00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:10.080
Oh, my God.
哦，天哪。

523
00:25:10.080 --> 00:25:11.380
And I was just teasing.
我只是在开玩笑。

524
00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:18.620
So now I want to go back to fun run deleted scenes and be like, I totally forgot that scene.
所以现在我想回去看欢乐跑的删减片段，然后心想，我完全忘了那一幕。

525
00:25:19.040 --> 00:25:25.280
Well, Greg told me that they went back to our old lot and they restored the Scranton Business
格雷格告诉我，他们回到了我们以前的外景地，并且为了开场建立镜头

526
00:25:25.280 --> 00:25:28.560
sign park for that opening establishing shot.
恢复了斯克兰顿商业园的招牌。

527
00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:35.260
And he said that on that day, some fans were there and they came and took photos.
他说那天有些粉丝在那里，他们过来拍了照片。

528
00:25:35.260 --> 00:25:39.220
He was like, they got really lucky because, you know, that sign is not usually there.
他当时说，他们真的很幸运，因为你知道，那个招牌通常不在那里。

529
00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:39.640
Right.
对。

530
00:25:39.640 --> 00:25:40.480
On the building.
在建筑上。

531
00:25:40.780 --> 00:25:43.820
He said it was just kind of cool to see it there again.
他说再次在那里看到它感觉挺酷的。

532
00:25:44.540 --> 00:25:52.040
But like Bobby said, the Vance refrigeration and the Eye Center and the elevator, all of that,
但就像鲍比说的，凡斯冷气公司、眼科中心和电梯，所有这些，

533
00:25:52.220 --> 00:25:56.100
they completely rebuilt on a soundstage at the Universal lot.
都是他们在环球影城外景地的摄影棚里完全重建的。

534
00:25:56.240 --> 00:25:59.880
Because that's where they shot the paper was on a soundstage at the Universal lot.
因为他们拍摄纸业公司的地方就是环球影城的一个摄影棚。

535
00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:00.740
That's right.
没。

536
00:26:00.800 --> 00:26:02.060
And we went and visited there.
我们去那里参观过。

537
00:26:02.800 --> 00:26:06.380
And, you know, we were walking to our cars at the end of the day.
而且，你知道，那天结束时我们正走向汽车。

538
00:26:06.520 --> 00:26:07.240
Greg was so sweet.
格雷格太贴心了。

539
00:26:07.360 --> 00:26:09.140
He walked us out after our visit.
我们参观完后他送我们出来。

540
00:26:09.700 --> 00:26:10.940
We're standing by the cars.
我们站在车旁。

541
00:26:11.100 --> 00:26:13.120
And one of those buses went by.
其中一辆观光车开了过去。

542
00:26:13.360 --> 00:26:14.700
Yeah, that Bobby talked about.
就是鲍比提到的那种。

543
00:26:14.700 --> 00:26:19.360
Yeah, it's like an open air bus with a bunch of visitors who are coming to Universal Studios.
对，就像那种露天巴士，上面坐着一群来环球影城参观的游客。

544
00:26:19.360 --> 00:26:20.420
You pay for this pass.
你买这种通行证。

545
00:26:20.540 --> 00:26:22.000
You get the tour of the whole back lot.
就能参观整个外景地。

546
00:26:22.180 --> 00:26:23.500
And there we were standing there.
而我们当时就站在那儿。

547
00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:25.720
And Greg literally was like, get down.
格雷格简直就像是说，趴下。

548
00:26:25.920 --> 00:26:26.620
Look at us.
看着我们。

549
00:26:26.960 --> 00:26:28.660
Dive behind like a dumpster.
像躲在垃圾桶后面一样扑过去。

550
00:26:29.080 --> 00:26:31.140
We literally dove behind a dumpster.
我们真的扑到了垃圾桶后面。

551
00:26:31.160 --> 00:26:31.320
Yeah.
是啊。

552
00:26:31.520 --> 00:26:34.140
Because we did not want people to see us there.
因为我们不想让别人看到我们在那儿。

553
00:26:34.240 --> 00:26:34.940
We were afraid.
我们很害怕。

554
00:26:35.120 --> 00:26:35.740
With Greg.
和格雷格一起。

555
00:26:36.040 --> 00:26:36.360
Yes.
对。

556
00:26:36.920 --> 00:26:39.960
Because there were the rumors that the paper was happening.
因为当时有传言说这部剧要开拍了。

557
00:26:40.300 --> 00:26:40.540
Yeah.
是啊。

558
00:26:41.260 --> 00:26:42.720
And we, yes.
而我们，没错。

559
00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:43.360
Yeah.
对。

560
00:26:43.360 --> 00:26:50.660
But I have to say, hearing now that people took pictures of that Scranton Park sign at our old set.
但我得说，现在听说有人拍下了我们旧片场那个斯克兰顿公园的标志。

561
00:26:50.820 --> 00:26:51.060
Yeah.
是啊。

562
00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:53.780
Guys, zoom in.
伙计们，放大看看。

563
00:26:53.880 --> 00:26:55.660
I bet you have laser one and done.
我敢说你们肯定一眼就能看出来。

564
00:26:56.300 --> 00:26:57.800
You probably do.
你们可能真的能。

565
00:26:58.540 --> 00:26:59.140
Yeah.
对。

566
00:26:59.620 --> 00:27:05.700
Well, now that our documentary crew has figured out that Dunder Mifflin was bought by Enervate,
好了，既然我们的纪录片摄制组已经发现邓德·米福林被恩维特收购了，

567
00:27:05.900 --> 00:27:07.220
we're going to go to Enervate.
我们要去恩维特了。

568
00:27:07.340 --> 00:27:08.140
To Toledo.
去托莱多。

569
00:27:08.420 --> 00:27:10.380
Yes, to the Truth Teller Tower.
没错，去“真言大厦”。

570
00:27:10.380 --> 00:27:17.620
And we go upstairs and we're going to see a bunch of workers in these like glass-walled cubicles.
我们上楼，会看到一群工人在那种玻璃墙的隔间里。

571
00:27:17.620 --> 00:27:18.020
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

572
00:27:18.700 --> 00:27:20.880
And one of them is shaving.
其中一个人在刮胡子。

573
00:27:21.060 --> 00:27:23.940
He's got an electric shaver and he's reclining, kind of shaving.
他拿着一个电动剃须刀，半躺着，一边刮胡子。

574
00:27:24.320 --> 00:27:27.880
He's getting the side eye from the person in the cubicle next to him.
旁边隔间的人正斜眼看他。

575
00:27:28.020 --> 00:27:28.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

576
00:27:28.980 --> 00:27:33.380
Shout out to Steven Socks, who played the man shaving his face.
向扮演那个刮脸男人的史蒂文·索克斯致敬。

577
00:27:33.380 --> 00:27:37.520
You might recognize that name because we have talked about him and his wife, Lori, for years.
你可能对这个名字很熟悉，因为我们谈论他和他的妻子洛瑞已经好几年了。

578
00:27:37.960 --> 00:27:40.460
They were the stand-in team on The Office.
他们曾是《办公室》的替身演员组。

579
00:27:40.820 --> 00:27:45.000
They both had cameos on The Office, and I was so tickled to see him on the paper.
他们俩都在《办公室》里客串过，看到他出现在这部剧里我太高兴了。

580
00:27:45.180 --> 00:27:46.120
Yes, lady.
没错，女士。

581
00:27:46.320 --> 00:27:52.740
When we visited, we saw both Steven and Lori, and it was so cool, but I had no idea that he had a cameo.
我们去探班时，见到了史蒂文和洛瑞，这太酷了，但我根本不知道他有客串。

582
00:27:52.800 --> 00:27:56.760
Neither did I because everybody locked it up.
我也不知道，因为大家都保密得严严实实的。

583
00:27:56.760 --> 00:28:00.580
So when we watched this, I texted him about working on the paper.
所以当我们看这部剧时，我给他发信息问了关于参演这部剧的事。

584
00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:06.880
I asked him how him and Lori came to work on the paper, what it was like working on the show, what it was like to do this cameo.
我问他和洛瑞是如何来参演这部剧的，在片场工作是什么感觉，客串的感觉怎么样。

585
00:28:07.360 --> 00:28:10.740
And he sent us the most lovely message, just like Bobby Ray.
他给我们发来了一段非常暖心的信息，就像鲍比·雷一样。

586
00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:12.500
Everyone has just been so wonderful.
每个人都太棒了。

587
00:28:12.780 --> 00:28:13.860
You got to hear it.
你们得听听这个。

588
00:28:15.160 --> 00:28:21.700
Lori and I both got to work on the paper, and the pilot episode was really a thrill.
我和洛瑞都有幸参与了这部剧，试播集真的让人非常激动。

589
00:28:21.700 --> 00:28:29.100
I mean, somehow, we were both able to work on The Office for all those years, and we made so many memories.
我是说，不知怎么的，我们竟然能在《办公室》工作了那么多年，留下了那么多回忆。

590
00:28:29.580 --> 00:28:41.500
And as soon as we found out about there even being a true Office spinoff, we reached out to Greg Daniels, who is just so kind and just absolutely brilliant.
而且一听说真的会有《办公室》的衍生剧，我们就联系了格雷格·丹尼尔斯，他不仅人非常好，而且绝对才华横溢。

591
00:28:41.700 --> 00:28:45.560
And somehow, we got to work on this brand new show.
不知怎么的，我们竟然又参与了这部全新的剧集。

592
00:28:46.180 --> 00:28:55.120
Well, one day, I had a break from filming, and I walked over to one of the other stages we were using, and I saw the outside of a set that had just been built.
有一天，我拍戏间隙休息，走到我们使用的另一个片场，看到刚刚搭建好的一处布景的外观。

593
00:28:56.000 --> 00:29:02.200
And from the outside, a set just looks like wood and nails and a door here and there.
从外面看，片场不过是木头、钉子和几扇门而已。

594
00:29:02.320 --> 00:29:08.000
And it's not until you open the door and step inside that the set is revealed.
直到你推开门走进去，布景才会展现出来。

595
00:29:08.860 --> 00:29:12.740
There was no one else, not a single person on the stage, and so I was all alone.
当时没有别人，片场里一个人也没有，所以我孤身一人。

596
00:29:12.740 --> 00:29:16.500
And I was curious about what we might shoot the next few days.
我很好奇接下来几天我们要拍什么。

597
00:29:16.740 --> 00:29:19.020
You know, it could have been a restaurant or an apartment or whatever.
你知道的，可能是一家餐厅、一间公寓什么的。

598
00:29:19.220 --> 00:29:26.760
So I opened one of the doors, and it was the office's elevator lobby.
于是我推开其中一扇门，发现那是办公室的电梯大堂。

599
00:29:27.620 --> 00:29:34.400
I had entered that door that was a stairwell door next to Bob Vance's glass door.
我走进的那扇门，正是鲍勃·凡斯玻璃门旁边的那个楼梯间门。

600
00:29:34.400 --> 00:29:42.040
And I was instantly taken back to the old Chandler Valley Studios in Van Nuys.
我瞬间被带回了位于范奈斯的钱德勒山谷旧片场。

601
00:29:42.560 --> 00:29:47.340
It was shocking and emotional, actually.
事实上，当时既震撼又充满情绪。

602
00:29:48.180 --> 00:29:52.980
I walked up to the elevator, and so many memories flooded my brain.
我走到电梯前，无数的回忆涌上心头。

603
00:29:52.980 --> 00:29:57.660
And I thought of one of the most vivid memories on the show.
我想起了剧中印象最深刻的一个场景。

604
00:29:57.660 --> 00:30:04.860
It was Steve Carell's last day, and specifically, Steve's last scene.
那是史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的最后一天，具体来说，是史蒂夫的最后一场戏。

605
00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:12.000
The scene was when Michael says goodbye to the office, and he walks to the elevator and exits the building.
这场戏是迈克尔向办公室告别，他走向电梯并离开大楼。

606
00:30:12.380 --> 00:30:19.160
The day before, Greg had asked me to wear a suit, and so he put me in the scene.
前一天，格雷格让我穿上一套西装，于是他把我安排进了这场戏。

607
00:30:19.580 --> 00:30:23.160
Me and a mail courier walk out of the elevator.
我和一个邮件快递员一起走出了电梯。

608
00:30:23.160 --> 00:30:32.360
As Michael walks in, on Steve's last take, I watched the character, Michael Scott, enter the elevator, and the doors closed.
当迈克尔走进来时，在史蒂夫的最后一条镜头中，我看着迈克尔·斯科特这个角色走进电梯，门关上了。

609
00:30:32.700 --> 00:30:38.980
And then after the scene ended, the doors opened, and the actor, Steve Carell, stepped out.
场景结束门打开后，演员史蒂夫·卡瑞尔走了出来。

610
00:30:39.680 --> 00:30:44.600
It really was just him and I in the lobby at that point, and I couldn't help myself, and I just gave him a big hug.
当时大厅里真的只有我和他两个人，我情不自禁地给了他一个大大的拥抱。

611
00:30:45.580 --> 00:30:49.940
Well, here I was, back in that space, and I had goosebumps.
就这样，我回到了那个地方，起了一身鸡皮疙瘩。

612
00:30:50.800 --> 00:30:58.920
I saw Bob Vance's office, and then I walked toward the Dunder Mifflin office, and it was a laser hair removal place.
我看到了鲍勃·万斯办公室，然后走向邓德·米弗林办公室，结果那里变成了一家激光脱毛店。

613
00:30:59.220 --> 00:31:02.500
So it was, Dunder Mifflin was gone.
所以，邓德·米弗林已经不复存在了。

614
00:31:04.040 --> 00:31:08.980
And what I felt at that moment was just closure.
我那一刻感受到的只有释怀。

615
00:31:10.160 --> 00:31:16.280
Life moves on, and art shows us in amazing ways that life has changed.
生活在继续，而艺术以惊人的方式向我们展现了生活的变迁。

616
00:31:17.380 --> 00:31:25.140
I got to stand there in that moment, full of gratitude for all that the office meant to me.
我在那一刻驻足，对《办公室》对我而言的一切充满了感激。

617
00:31:26.420 --> 00:31:31.480
And then in that same breath, I got to pivot to this brand new show.
与此同时，我又得以转向这部全新的剧集。

618
00:31:32.960 --> 00:31:41.040
And then, like, the next day, they asked me if I could come in and work with the talented Tim Key in one of the opening scenes of the pilot.
然后，就像是第二天，他们问我能不能来和才华横溢的蒂姆·基一起拍试播集的一个开场镜头。

619
00:31:42.620 --> 00:31:46.020
Just an incredible experience that I will never forget.
这是一次我永生难忘的不可思议的经历。

620
00:31:47.700 --> 00:31:49.040
That is so powerful.
太有感染力了。

621
00:31:49.800 --> 00:31:52.560
Well, I cried the first time I listened to that.
我第一次听的时候都哭了。

622
00:31:52.740 --> 00:31:53.000
Yeah.
是啊。

623
00:31:53.180 --> 00:32:00.100
Because he's right about what art can show us, and I just can't imagine what it was like.
因为他说得很对，关于艺术能向我们展现什么，我简直无法想象当时那种感觉是什么样的。

624
00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:01.860
Like, it feels like time travel.
感觉就像时间旅行一样。

625
00:32:01.980 --> 00:32:02.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

626
00:32:02.480 --> 00:32:06.580
If I could open a door and be standing in that elevator bay again.
如果我也能推开一扇门，重新站在那个电梯间里。

627
00:32:06.580 --> 00:32:11.100
And I didn't know that story, that he had that moment with Steve.
我以前不知道这个故事，不知道他和史蒂夫有过那样的一刻。

628
00:32:11.240 --> 00:32:11.500
Yeah.
是啊。

629
00:32:12.000 --> 00:32:20.280
And then now he is there again all these years later in that same elevator bay.
而现在，时隔多年，他又回到了那个相同的电梯间。

630
00:32:20.520 --> 00:32:24.400
And, yeah, I thought Stephen said it all so well.
是的，我觉得史蒂芬把这一切都表达得太好了。

631
00:32:24.540 --> 00:32:24.720
Yeah.
对。

632
00:32:24.860 --> 00:32:26.480
I felt everything that he shared.
他分享的每一种感受我都感同身受。

633
00:32:27.880 --> 00:32:29.200
You're a little teary.
你都有点想哭了。

634
00:32:29.440 --> 00:32:31.000
I, you know, yeah.
我，你知道的，对。

635
00:32:31.140 --> 00:32:34.760
It makes me so excited for this group of people.
这让我对这群演员充满期待。

636
00:32:34.760 --> 00:32:40.960
I just hope that this show gets to give them what The Office gave us.
我只希望这部剧能带给他们当年《办公室》带给我们的那种体验。

637
00:32:41.220 --> 00:32:41.380
Yeah.
是啊。

638
00:32:42.240 --> 00:32:42.720
All right.
好了。

639
00:32:42.900 --> 00:32:47.380
Well, now we are going to cut to a talking head of Ken.
那么，现在我们要切入肯的访谈镜头。

640
00:32:47.700 --> 00:32:49.300
Ken is played by Tim Key.
肯由蒂姆·基饰演。

641
00:32:49.580 --> 00:32:49.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

642
00:32:50.040 --> 00:32:50.920
He is British.
他是英国人。

643
00:32:50.920 --> 00:32:55.100
He is the head of strategy for the corporate offices at Enervate.
他是Enervate公司总部战略部负责人。

644
00:32:55.180 --> 00:32:58.680
And he's going to explain to us what Enervate does.
他将向我们解释Enervate是做什么的。

645
00:32:59.000 --> 00:32:59.900
Let's listen.
我们来听听。

646
00:33:01.900 --> 00:33:04.360
Enervate sells products made out of paper.
Enervate销售纸质产品。

647
00:33:04.760 --> 00:33:06.640
So that might be office supplies.
可能是办公用品。

648
00:33:06.880 --> 00:33:15.180
That might be janitorial paper, which is toilet tissue, toilet seat protectors, and local newspapers.
也可能是保洁用纸，也就是卫生纸、马桶垫纸以及当地报纸。

649
00:33:15.420 --> 00:33:17.620
And that is in order of quality.
按质量从高到低排列。

650
00:33:20.560 --> 00:33:25.320
I loved at the very end when he says in order of quality, he thinks he's being funny.
我特别喜欢最后他说“按质量从高到低排列”的时候，他觉得自己挺搞笑的。

651
00:33:25.480 --> 00:33:25.620
Yeah.
是啊。

652
00:33:25.660 --> 00:33:29.660
And he has this little smirk look to camera, and it just cracked me up.
他对着镜头露出了那种微微的假笑，真的把我逗笑了。

653
00:33:30.100 --> 00:33:32.440
Now he's going to take us on the tour of the offices.
现在他要带我们参观办公室了。

654
00:33:33.360 --> 00:33:36.100
He explains that the corporate offices are on the eighth floor.
他解释说公司办公室在八楼。

655
00:33:36.260 --> 00:33:38.340
He's going to take us up to the ninth floor.
他要带我们去九楼。

656
00:33:38.340 --> 00:33:38.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

657
00:33:38.960 --> 00:33:47.680
This reminded me of our pilot where Michael Scott is taking you on a tour of Dunder Mifflin because he starts introducing everybody.
这让我想起了我们的试播集，迈克尔·斯科特带你参观邓德米弗林，因为他开始介绍每一个人。

658
00:33:47.880 --> 00:33:47.980
Yep.
没错。

659
00:33:47.980 --> 00:33:53.520
So we find out that the ninth floor is home to Softie's toilet paper.
所以我们发现九楼是软萌卷纸（Softie's）的所在地。

660
00:33:53.520 --> 00:33:58.000
And when he opens the door, by the way, this is when we get our first glimpse of the set.
当他打开门的时候，顺便说一下，我们就是在这个时候第一次看到了片场。

661
00:33:58.120 --> 00:33:59.540
And it is huge.
而且它太大了。

662
00:33:59.540 --> 00:34:01.460
It's so vaSt.
极其广阔。

663
00:34:01.780 --> 00:34:02.040
Yes.
对。

664
00:34:02.260 --> 00:34:05.280
It is this big open space, but there are very few people in it.
这是一个巨大的开放空间，但里面的人很少。

665
00:34:05.380 --> 00:34:05.680
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

666
00:34:06.120 --> 00:34:11.080
Michael Komen told me that this scene was the very first scene they shot of the paper.
迈克尔·科门告诉我，这场戏是他们拍这部剧的第一场戏。

667
00:34:11.160 --> 00:34:11.720
Oh, really?
哦，真的吗？

668
00:34:11.900 --> 00:34:12.160
Yes.
是的。

669
00:34:12.320 --> 00:34:12.580
Aw.
噢。

670
00:34:13.160 --> 00:34:21.200
Well, you know, as Ken walks through, he's greeting his toilet kings and one queen, who I think has a little bit of an Angela Martin vibe.
你知道的，当肯走过时，他在向他的卷纸之王们以及唯一的女王打招呼，我觉得她有点安吉拉·马丁的风格。

671
00:34:21.360 --> 00:34:21.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

672
00:34:21.660 --> 00:34:23.820
She's got that ponytail pulled back tight.
她扎着紧紧的马尾辫。

673
00:34:24.160 --> 00:34:28.160
And I love the throwaway snarky comment Ken said as he walked past her.
我很喜欢肯走过她身边时顺口说出的那句讽刺的话。

674
00:34:28.160 --> 00:34:33.940
He says, scrunchie, no harm in it because she has her hair in a scrunchie.
他说，发圈，没什么大不了的，因为她用发圈扎着头发。

675
00:34:34.120 --> 00:34:36.300
It was just a really funny throwaway line.
这只是一句非常有趣的随口台词。

676
00:34:36.920 --> 00:34:38.860
Well, scrunchie gal, a.k.a.
好吧，发圈妹，也就是

677
00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:41.360
Toilet Queen, is our first writer-performer.
卷纸女王，是我们第一位编剧兼演员。

678
00:34:41.500 --> 00:34:47.700
She is a character that we're going to see at Softie's named Kimberly, and she is played by Mo Welch.
她是我们在软萌卷纸里会看到的一个角色，名叫金伯利，由莫·韦尔奇饰演。

679
00:34:48.160 --> 00:34:51.740
Ken continues now to show us the rest of the Softie's side of the office.
肯现在继续带我们参观办公室里软萌卷纸的另一侧。

680
00:34:51.740 --> 00:34:54.560
There's a lot of old artwork and logos.
有很多旧的艺术品和标志。

681
00:34:54.560 --> 00:34:59.940
And then he takes us to a gong that they hit whenever a sale is made.
然后他带我们去看一面锣，只要达成一笔销售他们就会敲响它。

682
00:34:59.940 --> 00:35:04.340
I have to imagine that's going to drive everyone crazy if you work there.
我不得不想象，如果你在那里工作，那会把每个人都逼疯的。

683
00:35:05.500 --> 00:35:14.280
And this is when he introduces us to what's on the other side of the office, which is the local newspaper, the Toledo Truth Teller.
也就是在这个时候，他向我们介绍了办公室另一侧的东西，也就是当地的报纸《托莱多真理报》。

684
00:35:14.280 --> 00:35:15.020
Yes.
对。

685
00:35:15.260 --> 00:35:17.400
We find out that this entire building—
我们发现整栋大楼——

686
00:35:17.400 --> 00:35:18.480
Which is a big building.
这是一栋很大的建筑。

687
00:35:18.480 --> 00:35:18.960
Yes.
是的。

688
00:35:19.140 --> 00:35:23.740
It used to house the newspaper with a staff of like a thousand.
它以前是一家员工大约有一千人的报社所在地。

689
00:35:24.380 --> 00:35:29.120
And now they're just like half of this floor, and there's like seven of them.
而现在他们只占了这一层的一半，大概只有七个人。

690
00:35:29.220 --> 00:35:29.540
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

691
00:35:30.020 --> 00:35:32.380
Then we flash back to 1971.
然后我们闪回到1971年。

692
00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:35.260
Yeah, we're going to watch a little black-and-white documentary.
对，我们要看一小段黑白纪录片。

693
00:35:35.620 --> 00:35:36.900
That's the year I was born.
那是我的出生年份。

694
00:35:36.900 --> 00:35:40.840
Guys, we did have color TV in 1971.
伙计们，1971年我们确实有彩色电视。

695
00:35:42.500 --> 00:35:44.440
I am not that old.
我没有那么老。

696
00:35:44.960 --> 00:35:46.320
I am 54.
我54岁。

697
00:35:47.100 --> 00:35:48.360
You're so right.
你说得太对了。

698
00:35:48.620 --> 00:35:49.980
It made me laugh.
这把我逗笑了。

699
00:35:51.400 --> 00:35:52.080
Anyway.
言归正传。

700
00:35:52.620 --> 00:35:59.140
I think we just needed to differentiate between our current day story and this like documentary.
我想我们只是需要区分我们当下的故事和这个类似纪录片的东西。

701
00:36:00.520 --> 00:36:01.200
Okay.
好吧。

702
00:36:01.200 --> 00:36:02.200
But you're so right.
但你真的说得太对了。

703
00:36:02.460 --> 00:36:06.520
Anyway, I'm sure that's exactly why they did it, but it did crack me up.
不管怎样，我确信这正是他们这么做的原因，但真的把我逗乐了。

704
00:36:07.160 --> 00:36:07.620
Yes.
是的。

705
00:36:07.860 --> 00:36:14.960
So we're watching this old documentary, and it's being hosted by John Stack, the publisher
所以我们当时在看一部老纪录片，由《托莱多真相报》

706
00:36:14.960 --> 00:36:17.100
of the Toledo Truth Teller.
的出版商约翰·斯塔克主持。

707
00:36:17.300 --> 00:36:23.000
And we're seeing our same set, but now it is just filled with like wall-to-wall people.
我们看到了同样的布景，但现在里面挤满了人，水泄不通。

708
00:36:23.380 --> 00:36:23.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

709
00:36:24.080 --> 00:36:26.760
John Stack is played by Tracy Letts.
约翰·斯塔克由特雷西·莱茨饰演。

710
00:36:27.140 --> 00:36:27.480
Lady.
天哪。

711
00:36:28.020 --> 00:36:28.480
Lady.
天哪。

712
00:36:28.820 --> 00:36:32.560
Oh, your theater nerd heart went into overdrive.
哦，你内心的戏剧迷之魂瞬间燃爆了。

713
00:36:32.720 --> 00:36:33.800
You were like, Angela.
你当时就像是在说，安吉拉。

714
00:36:34.180 --> 00:36:34.500
Ah.
啊。

715
00:36:34.780 --> 00:36:35.040
Angela.
安吉拉。

716
00:36:36.640 --> 00:36:38.420
He was multiple Tony Award winner.
他曾多次获得托尼奖。

717
00:36:38.660 --> 00:36:40.640
He wrote August to Osage County.
他写过《八月：奥色治郡》。

718
00:36:40.880 --> 00:36:45.660
He won a Tony for playing George in the revival of Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf.
他因在重排版《谁害怕弗吉尼亚·伍尔芙》中饰演乔治而赢得托尼奖。

719
00:36:45.720 --> 00:36:46.580
I saw it.
我看过。

720
00:36:46.760 --> 00:36:49.080
I saw all of it.
我全看了。

721
00:36:49.080 --> 00:36:55.500
I went to Chicago to see his play, Superior Donuts, at Steppenwolf, and lady, afterwards,
我特意去芝加哥的荒原狼剧团看他的话剧《高级甜甜圈》，天哪，演出结束后，

722
00:36:55.840 --> 00:36:57.920
I got to go out and have drinks with him.
我有幸和他一起出去喝了酒。

723
00:36:58.120 --> 00:36:58.540
Wow.
哇。

724
00:36:59.040 --> 00:37:00.260
Did you keep your cool?
你当时表现得很淡定吗？

725
00:37:00.520 --> 00:37:02.120
Did you say anything ridiculous?
有没有说出什么荒唐的话？

726
00:37:02.400 --> 00:37:02.680
Or were you—
还是说你——

727
00:37:02.680 --> 00:37:03.480
I barely spoke.
我几乎没怎么说话。

728
00:37:03.620 --> 00:37:03.780
Okay.
好吧。

729
00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:04.340
That's smart.
那很明智。

730
00:37:04.440 --> 00:37:05.200
That's smart.
那很明智。

731
00:37:05.200 --> 00:37:07.000
I was so nervous.
我当时太紧张了。

732
00:37:07.000 --> 00:37:07.220
In awe.
肃然起敬。

733
00:37:07.560 --> 00:37:07.940
Yes.
是的。

734
00:37:08.120 --> 00:37:08.480
Yes.
是的。

735
00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:15.180
So I asked Michael Komen, I was like, how did you get Tracy Letts on the show?
所以我问迈克尔·科门，我说，你是怎么请到特雷西·莱茨来演这个节目的？

736
00:37:15.180 --> 00:37:19.440
And Michael Komen was like, as big of a nerd about him as I was.
迈克尔·科门说，他对他的崇拜丝毫不亚于我。

737
00:37:19.540 --> 00:37:21.120
And he said he was my first choice.
他说他是我的首选。

738
00:37:21.680 --> 00:37:23.040
So they just reached out.
所以他们就联系了他。

739
00:37:23.260 --> 00:37:24.440
And he said yes.
而他答应了。

740
00:37:24.540 --> 00:37:28.240
And Michael was like, I was genuinely thrilled.
迈克尔说，我当时真的激动坏了。

741
00:37:28.500 --> 00:37:32.800
Well, now the scene that's going to come at the end makes perfect sense to me.
好吧，现在结尾要播出的那个场景对我来说完全说得通了。

742
00:37:32.940 --> 00:37:33.120
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

743
00:37:33.300 --> 00:37:34.040
We'll get to that.
我们一会儿会聊到那儿。

744
00:37:34.200 --> 00:37:34.840
We'll get to it.
我们一会儿会聊到。

745
00:37:35.000 --> 00:37:36.400
Because of Michael's love of him.
因为迈克尔太崇拜他了。

746
00:37:36.400 --> 00:37:38.600
Well, he absolutely adores him.
嗯，他是真的非常崇拜他。

747
00:37:38.740 --> 00:37:41.480
He said they actually shot a ton of stuff with him.
他说他们实际上拍了大量关于他的素材。

748
00:37:41.580 --> 00:37:46.820
And he really hopes that they're going to be able to keep weaving this old, quote-unquote, documentary.
他真心希望他们能够继续把这部所谓的、年代久远的老纪录片穿插进去。

749
00:37:47.180 --> 00:37:48.380
From 1971.
来自1971年。

750
00:37:48.900 --> 00:37:50.560
This old black and white documentary.
这部老黑白纪录片。

751
